# Keeps the Docker build context small. Without this file, `docker build`/`docker compose
# build` sends the entire repo (~7GB+, mostly data/ and outputs/) to the daemon before any build
# step runs. None of the excluded paths below are needed inside the API or dashboard images --
# in local dev, docker-compose.override.yml bind-mounts ./data and ./outputs over the image at
# runtime (restoring the previous default `docker compose up` behavior); the production-lean
# base docker-compose.yml has no such mounts and doesn't need this data to build or boot (see
# apps/api/main.py's graceful fallback when outputs/max_recall_system_summary.json is absent).

.git
.github
data/raw
data/processed
data/features
.env
.claude

__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
.venv
venv
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# Generated/large artifacts and pickled models -- neither service loads models/*.pkl directly
# (API works on precomputed scores; dashboard reads OOF/prediction parquets, not model files).
outputs/
models/

# Documentation and research artifacts -- not read by either service at runtime.
docs/
results/
*.md
